From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:07:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Silicon/Spacemit/K3: add AcpiClockInitDxe for OS-visible
 clock bring-up

Under ACPI the OS has no clock driver, so firmware must leave every
OS-driven device-block clock in a working state at handoff. This
driver idempotently enables, at ReadyToBoot, the clocks of ACPI
device blocks that no UEFI device driver owns (and therefore nothing
else leaves clocked): TSEN (thermal sensor) and ESPI (the eSPI master
for the ChromeOS EC). GMAC/PCIe/USB are deliberately not re-asserted:
their UEFI device drivers already enable them during BDS connect.

History: an earlier revision also re-asserted GMAC/PCIe/USB and
caused a boot-reset loop; the actual cause was the ClockDxe
ConfigNum/row corruption fixed in the preceding commit, but the
minimal bring-up set is kept deliberately.

Clock names must match ClockDxe's ModuleConfig[] exactly.
